### Welcome Mac to the Lab!

We’re excited to welcome **Mac** to the lab as he joins us for his postdoctoral work starting **July 1st**!

Mac holds an **M.S. in Biology** from the **University of Colorado Denver** and recently completed his **Ph.D. in Evolutionary Biology** at the **University of Pennsylvania**. His doctoral research focused on the **genomics of seasonality and diapause** in *Rhagoletis pomonella*, and more recently, he has been exploring **plant–microbe interactions** at the molecular level.

We’re thrilled to have Mac bring his expertise in **evolutionary genomics** and **host–microbiome dynamics** to the team. Welcome aboard!


### Welcome Amartya to the Lab!

We’re happy to welcome **Amartya Nalluri** to the lab as a visiting undergraduate researcher starting **May 20**!

Amartya is currently a **sophomore at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign**, majoring in **Integrative Biology Honors** with a minor in **Statistics**. He works in **Dr. Heath’s lab** in the Department of Plant Biology, where he has explored **plant–microbe coevolution** and conducted experiments on **barcoded Sinorhizobium strains** in *Medicago truncatula*. His work has included plant phenotyping, microbial preparation, and species identification for large-scale greenhouse experiments.

Beyond the lab, Amartya is a **Senior Copy Editor at The Daily Illini** and enjoys writing short stories and exploring the vibrant food scene of Champaign-Urbana. Originally from **Midtown Manhattan**, he’s joining us for the summer to deepen his research experience closer to home.

We’re excited to have him with us this summer—welcome, Amartya!


### Welcome Michael to the Lab!

We’re excited to welcome **Michael (Md Nafis um Alam)** to the lab for the summer, starting **June 9**!

Michael is currently a **PhD student at the Arizona Genomics Institute** in the **School of Plant Sciences**, where he works under the mentorship of **Dr. Rod A. Wing**. Originally from **Bangladesh**, Michael earned his undergraduate degree in **Biochemistry and Molecular Biology** from the **University of Dhaka**. His broad research interests lie in **evolutionary biology**.

This summer, Michael will be collaborating with **Hanna** on the **comparative R gene project**, focusing on **polyploid species like *Draba verna***. His work centers on **genome assembly** as part of the lab’s broader efforts to understand the evolution and function of plant immune genes.

He’ll be with us through **mid-August**, and we’re thrilled to have him on board—welcome, Michael!



### Welcome Em to the Lab!

We’re excited to welcome **Em Schissler**, who joined the lab on **April 1st**!

Em earned a **B.A. in Biology** from **Occidental College**, focusing on **zoology**, and went on to complete an **M.S. in Biology** with a concentration in **bioinformatics and systems biology** at **New York University**. Their graduate work included analyzing the population decline of *Phoenix theophrasti* and contributing to Alzheimer’s research at **NYU Langone**, helping develop new diagnostic and treatment strategies.

Currently, Em supports the lab by managing **grant administration** and other **administrative responsibilities**, and also collaborates with postdoctoral researchers on **computational biology projects**.

Outside the lab, Em brings a deep passion for **animal care**, with experience working with both exotic and domestic species. In their free time, they love going to the **theater** and **rock climbing**.

Welcome, Em!
